Each entry gives, where applicable: title, author/maintainer, source link, and
license. "Derived/extracted" means Dilemma uses data computed from the source
(e.g. form-to-lemma pairs, headword lists, token statistics) rather than
redistributing the source verbatim.


Lexica and dictionaries
-----------------------

- English Wiktionary and Greek Wiktionary (Wikimedia community).
  https://en.wiktionary.org/ , https://el.wiktionary.org/
  Obtained as JSONL via kaikki.org (https://kaikki.org/).
  License: CC BY-SA 3.0  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/).
  Glosses and inflection data are extracted and transformed.

  The optional verb_subjects.json table extracts explicitly labeled usage
  restrictions from both editions via Kaikki/Wiktextract. It preserves source
  links, sense identifiers, labels, and snapshot hashes. The extracted and
  transformed table is distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/), matching the current
  Wiktionary text license. Its license is separate from the MIT source code.

- A Greek-English Lexicon (LSJ), H.G. Liddell, R. Scott, H.S. Jones,
  9th ed. (Oxford, 1940). Public domain. Headwords, forms, and POS via the
  LSJ9 processed exports (https://github.com/ciscoriordan/lsj9).

- Greek Lexicon of the Roman and Byzantine Periods, E.A. Sophocles.
  Public domain. TEI via Ionian University / Internet Archive
  (https://archive.org/details/pateres).

- Perseus Digital Library lexica - Lewis & Short, Pape, Bailly (headword
  filter only). https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/

- Diccionario Griego-Espanol (DGE), CSIC (headwords only).
  http://dge.cchs.csic.es/

- Lexicon of Greek Personal Names (LGPN), University of Oxford (proper names
  only). https://www.lgpn.ox.ac.uk/

- Dictionary of Standard Modern Greek (Triantafyllidis), Institute for Modern
  Greek Studies, via the Greek Language Portal and the glossAPI/EELLAK export
  on Mozilla Data Collective.
  https://www.greek-language.gr/greekLang/modern_greek/tools/lexica/triantafyllides/
  https://mozilladatacollective.com/datasets/cmo1sklpo00d0mk07taoepe1a
  The dataset listing declares CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 for the packaged export.
  Dilemma reads and ships only the factual bare headword strings from its
  `lemma` column; it does not read or redistribute definitions, examples,
  pronunciation, grammatical information, etymology, or source-page content.

- A Lexicon of the Homeric Dialect, R.J. Cunliffe. Public domain. Headwords
  and grammatical information expanded into paradigms with Wiktionary's
  grc-decl and grc-conj modules.

- Vocabolario della Lingua Greca (F. Montanari), Words in Progress
  (Aristarchus; F. Montanari, S. Perrone), and A Greek-English Lexicon,
  10th ed. (Liddell, Scott, Jones): bare headword strings only, used as
  lookup self-maps. Definitions and other dictionary content are not read
  or redistributed.

- A lexicon of Byzantine Greek (literary vocabulary of the 9th-12th c.):
  bare headword strings and genders only. The headwords are lookup
  self-maps, and their paradigms are generated with Wiktionary's grc-decl and
  grc-conj modules (build/expand_lbg.py). Definitions and other lexicon
  content are not read or redistributed.

- Nestle 1904 Greek New Testament, lowfat syntax trees. License: CC BY 4.0.
  Koine form-lemma pairs, lookup gap-fill only.

data/lookup_sources.json maps every input of lookup.db to the sources above
and their licenses; each lookup.db row names its source (see docs/usage.md).
Where pinned records tell the layers of a merged file apart, a row names the
layer: Wiktionary's own tables, the paradigms generated from LSJ, Sophocles
and Cunliffe headwords, or Modern Greek forms generated by rule.


