A note on source licensing
--------------------------

Every source of copyright-bearing text or annotation in Dilemma's shipped data
and models is openly licensed: no NonCommercial text, dictionary entries, or
treebank annotation is included. The Triantafyllidis reference inventory above
is limited to factual bare headword strings; the source's CC BY-NC-ND packaged
dictionary content is not ingested. The PROIEL treebank (CC BY-NC-SA, with no
permissive release) is excluded entirely. The Ancient Greek Dependency
Treebank is taken from the Perseus AGDT original (CC BY-SA 3.0 US), not the
NonCommercial Universal Dependencies repackaging (UD_Ancient_Greek-Perseus).
Diorisis is CC BY 4.0; the Gorman treebanks (CC BY-SA 4.0) are deliberately
never ingested - they are the held-out evaluation gold corpus, and the GLAUx
sentences whose manual trees were sourced from Gorman are skipped for the same
reason. The 25 GLAUx works whose treebank annotations derive from the PROIEL
treebank (CC BY-NC-SA: the New Testament books and Herodotus) are excluded
entirely. The handful of NonCommercial
source texts within GLAUx, and the per-file NonCommercial texts within the
Patristic Text Archive, are filtered out at build time (see build/nc_filter.py).
What Dilemma extracts from any treebank is factual form-to-lemma annotation and
aggregate token statistics, not the syntactic apparatus.

The shipped Modern Greek POS / dependency tagger is trained on UD_Greek-GUD
(CC BY-SA 4.0) plus the CC BY-SA dialect treebanks, NOT on UD_Greek-GDT, which
is CC BY-NC-SA. The Modern Greek lemmatizer model is built from Wiktionary and
the HNC Golden Corpus; the Triantafyllidis headwords affect convention
validation/remapping and give a listed headword its own lookup key, and do
not train that model.
